{"key":"NotesWindow","text":"## NotesWindow\n\nThe **Notes Window** is a markdown editor with GitHub sync, undo/redo,\nand a rich-text preview mode.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.15, 0.04 | Right-click to rename the window title or save filename. Turns cyan when there are unsaved changes. Click Edit to switch to the raw markdown editor, Done (or Ctrl+S) to save and return to view mode.\nContent Area | 0.50, 0.55 | In View mode, markdown renders as styled rich text (headings, bold, italic, bullets, horizontal rules). In Edit mode, type raw markdown. Ctrl+S saves; Escape cancels without saving. Click ⇄ to toggle word wrap.\n\n---\n\n### View / Edit Modes\n\n- **View mode** (default) — renders markdown as styled rich text\n- Click **Edit** to switch to the raw markdown editor\n- Click **Done** (or press `Ctrl+S`) to save and return to view mode\n\n---\n\n### Markdown Support\n\n| Syntax | Renders As |\n|---|---|\n| `# Heading` | Large bold heading |\n| `## Subheading` | Medium bold heading |\n| `**bold**` | Bold text |\n| `*italic*` | Italic text |\n| `- item` | Bullet point (•) |\n| `---` | Horizontal rule |\n\n---\n\n### Text Wrap\n\nClick the **⇄** button to toggle word wrap.\n\n- **On** (default) — text wraps within the window; vertical scroll only\n- **Off** — long lines scroll horizontally; useful for tables or code blocks\n\n---\n\n### Keyboard Shortcuts\n\n- `Ctrl+S` — save (while editing)\n- `Escape` — cancel edit without saving\n\n---\n\n### GitHub Sync\n\nNotes are automatically loaded from GitHub on open and saved on Done.\nIf GitHub is unavailable a yellow warning banner appears with a **Retry** button.\nThe note is also kept in StreamingAssets as a local fallback.\n\n---","screenshot":""}